<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simone Boccanegra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1363">1363</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simone Boccanegra was the first doge of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, elected for life in 1339 after a popular revolt against the noble families. He abdicated in 1344, returned as doge in 1356 and died, reputedly poisoned, in 1363. His life inspired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi">Verdi</a>'s opera Simon Boccanegra.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simone-boccanegra.jpg" alt="Simone Boccanegra" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlo Dell'Orto · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museo_di_Sant%27Agostino_(Genova)_Monumento_sepolcrale_di_Simone_Boccanegra_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
